msgstr "[Trascrizione (ENG)](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-Henchmen)"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/seeds/the-miners/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Miners"
msgstr "I Minatori"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-miners/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> A powerful co-op of rare earth miners, who long ago fought their owners and won, now face a new challenge: how to avoid becoming like them, knowing that without their work very few people will be able to produce electronics.\n"
msgstr "> Un potente sindacato di minatori di terre rare che hanno vinto le dispute con i proprietari anni addietro. Ora devono affrontare una sfida ben più grande: non diventare come loro, con la consapevolezza che senza il loro operato in pochi riusciranno a produrre componenti elettroniche.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-miners/index.en.md
msgid "[Solarpunk Prompts Podcast Episode](https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-miners)"
msgstr "[Episodio Solarpunk Prompts Podcast Episode](https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-miners)"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-miners/index.en.md
msgid "[Transcript](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-Miners)"
msgstr "[Trascrizione](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-Miners)"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/seeds/the-moonshot/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Moonshot"
msgstr "L'Allunaggio"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-moonshot/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> A group of scientists, environmentalists, and politicians, such as lobbyists to the UN, are analyzing the footprints of the solar panels and windmills around the world, trying to answer the question: is sending a rocket to the moon and back to get a tonne of moon soil the best thing we can do in the middle of a climate crisis? Is moon helium fusion the best way forward?\n"
msgstr "> Un’équipe di scienziati, ambientalisti e politici alla corte delle Nazioni Unite analizza i parametri di pannelli solari e turbine eoliche per rispondere a una domanda cruciale: è possibile lanciare un razzo sulla Luna per estrarre una tonnellata di suolo lunare? Se sì, è un modo utile di usare le risorse limitate nel bel mezzo della crisi climatica? La fusione di elio lunare è un incentivo sufficiente?\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-moonshot/index.en.md
msgid "[Solarpunk Prompts Podcast Episode](https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-moonshot)"
msgstr "[Episodio Solarpunk Prompts Podcast](https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-moonshot)"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-moonshot/index.en.md
msgid "[Transcript](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-Moonshot)"
msgstr "[Trascrizione (ENG)](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-Moonshot)"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Non-Economists"
msgstr "I Non-Economisti"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> A small team of researchers is woken up by their notification inboxes exploding: their mundane and unexciting report might have just started an economic war between multiple regions and communities. In a world with tightly-controlled carbon budgets, the production, use and recycling of every product is a subject of LCA, or a LifeCycle Assessment. A bad result might change the design, or move the production to another region, with potential political consequences. How will the researchers deal with their newly acquired (in)fame? Will they trust their analysis, buckle under pressure, or decide to play politics?\n"
msgstr "> Un piccolo team di ricercatori si sveglia con le caselle di posta in fiamme: il loro report noioso e di routine potrebbe aver innescato una guerra economica tra varie regioni e comunità. In un mondo di budget carbonici strettamente controllati, produzione, uso e riciclo di ogni prodotto è oggetto di un LCA, o Life Cycle Assessment. Un cattivo risultato può cambiarne il design o spostare la produzione in una regione diversa, con potenziali conseguenze politiche. Come faranno i ricercatori ad affrontare la loro nuova nomea? Si fideranno delle proprie analisi, capitoleranno sotto la pressione o decideranno di lanciarsi nei giochi politici?\n"

#. type: Title ##
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Raw Research Notes"
msgstr "Testo Originale delle Note:"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "What we have then - whether in terms of Carbon Credits, LCAs or other aspects - is a question how to structure a system to make sense and be unhackable."
msgstr "What we have then - whether in terms of Carbon Credits, LCAs or other aspects - is a question how to structure a system to make sense and be unhackable."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "One solution would be maximum transparency and treating the whole LCA process: the knowledge base, algorithms, specific decisions as a wiki, where everybody can look into and comment. How much can we offload on citizen scientists and citizen economists, however?"
msgstr "One solution would be maximum transparency and treating the whole LCA process: the knowledge base, algorithms, specific decisions as a wiki, where everybody can look into and comment. How much can we offload on citizen scientists and citizen economists, however?"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "This will also lead to faction wars, both in terms of ideology and economics. Every decision will have consequences - and even without layers of red tape and sleazy CEOs people can be rallied to vote against something important. What if the calculations show that - for example - India should not produce steel, which could be picked up by another, much smaller country? The sheer population and number of votes can out-weight it! Will they then vote on a flawed calculation method, led by a demagogue?"
msgstr "This will also lead to faction wars, both in terms of ideology and economics. Every decision will have consequences - and even without layers of red tape and sleazy CEOs people can be rallied to vote against something important. What if the calculations show that - for example - India should not produce steel, which could be picked up by another, much smaller country? The sheer population and number of votes can out-weigh it! Will they then vote on a flawed calculation method, led by a demagogue?"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "The bribes don't need to be financial. They can be prestige, acceptance by a faction, or whatever else."
msgstr "The bribes don't need to be financial. They can be prestige, acceptance by a faction, or whatever else."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "This prompt ties in with [the Miners](/seeds/the-miners), [The Moonshot](/seeds/the-moonshot) and many others."
msgstr "This prompt ties in with the Miners, The Moonshot and many others."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "Let's look for a story in it though:"
msgstr "Let's look for a story in it though:"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "Let's imagine a group of LCA scientists who just published just another analysis, being abruptly woken by their notification inboxes exploding. They were just launched on the front lines of a faction war, where their report was the \"last straw\" and might now contribute do a huge societal change, removing whole sectors of economy from one region of the world into another. Do they trust their work? Will they buckle under pressure? It's a good opportunity to walk the reader through how the LCA process looks like."
msgstr "Let's imagine a group of LCA scientists who just published just another analysis, being abruptly woken by their notification inboxes exploding. They were just launched on the front lines of a faction war, where their report was the \"last straw\" and might now contribute do a huge societal change, removing whole sectors of economy from one region of the world into another. Do they trust their work? Will they buckle under pressure? It's a good opportunity to walk the reader through how the LCA process looks like."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "Consider the world to be more anarchist, less hierarchical, where a lot of decisions are consensus-based and a subject of public debate, flames and online brigading. The scientists behind this report are now celebrities, widely known, whether they want it or not. If you want to cite a book with similar themes, you can go with LX Beckett's \"Gamechanger\" or \"Dealbreaker\", where the popular support for eco-policies is one of the most important plots of both novels."
msgstr "Consider the world to be more anarchist, less hierarchical, where a lot of decisions are consensus-based and a subject of public debate, flames and online brigading. The scientists behind this report are now celebrities, widely known, whether they want it or not. If you want to cite a book with similar themes, you can go with LX Beckett's \"Gamechanger\" or \"Dealbreaker\", where the popular support for eco-policies is one of the most important plots of both novels."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "Let's remember that more and more LCA processes are not just about energy and material, but are trying to count-in the uncountable, the effects on human happiness and labour practices. Yes, we could move the industry to China, but the general economic effect will produce X more tons of CO2, even if the factories will be more efficient."
msgstr "Let's remember that more and more LCA processes are not just about energy and material, but are trying to count-in the uncountable, the effects on human happiness and labour practices. Yes, we could move the industry to China, but the general economic effect will produce X more tons of CO2, even if the factories will be more efficient."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "Original notes:"
msgstr "Original notes:"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "If they aren’t careful, they could become like the economists of the past centuries, worshiping a mathematical model and a paradigm, instead of continuously testing it."
msgstr "If they aren’t careful, they could become like the economists of the past centuries, worshiping a mathematical model and a paradigm, instead of continuously testing it."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "Struggles of morality are ongoing in solarpunk"
msgstr "Struggles of morality are ongoing in solarpunk"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "Sources:"
msgstr "Sources:"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life-cycle_assessment"
msgstr "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life-cycle_assessment"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "We can throw in the https://globalcarbonreward.org/ and let's say, \"good faith\", non-blockchain carbon counting systems. We WILL need one."
msgstr "We can throw in the https://globalcarbonreward.org/ and let's say, \"good faith\", non-blockchain carbon counting systems. We WILL need one."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/seeds/the-pharmacists/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Pharmacists"
msgstr "I Farmacisti"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-pharmacists/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> A motley collection of neo-archeologists, data experts, doctors and biohackers are going through databases of the fallen pharmaceutical corporations, looking for drugs and solutions which worked, but were too cheap for the company giants to market. With so many medicines and procedures gone or extremely hard to get, maybe this is the best chance to rediscover cures?\n"
msgstr "> Una gang di neo-archeologi, esperti di dati, dottori e bioingegneri passa in rassegna gli archivi di aziende farmaceutiche fallite alla ricerca di medicine e soluzioni che funzionano ma non sono mai state diffuse perché troppo economiche per ricavarne profitti. Con così tante medicine scomparse o ardue da riprodurre, forse questa è la strada migliore per trovare nuove cure?\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-pharmacists/index.en.md
msgid "[Solarpunk Prompts Podcast Episode](https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-pharmacists)"
msgstr "[Episodio Solarpunk Prompts Podcast](https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-pharmacists)"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-pharmacists/index.en.md
msgid "[Transcript](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-Pharmacists)"
msgstr "[Trascrizione (ENG)](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-Pharmacists)"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Priorities"
msgstr "Le Priorità"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> A team of architects and civil engineers working on future-proofing their community need to make a hard decision. They are trying to prioritize the threats, but it’s a gamble trying to balance effectiveness and accessibility. They could make sure that one block won’t get flooded, but another district would need to wait.\n"
msgstr "> Una squadra di architetti e ingegneri civili all’opera per costruire un piano di sicurezza cittadina a prova di catastrofe deve prendere decisioni difficili per capire a quali minacce dare priorità. La sfida più grande è equilibrare l’efficacia e l’accessibilità delle loro soluzioni.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "Continuing the architecture and infrastructure again, this time from the perspective of the architects. This can be a pre-solarpunk or solarpunk endeavor, shown as more reactionary in the chaos of everything, or more of a \"good practice\" after decades of notes and hard decisions already made."
msgstr "Continuing the architecture and infrastructure again, this time from the perspective of the architects. This can be a pre-solarpunk or solarpunk endeavor, shown as more reactionary in the chaos of everything, or more of a \"good practice\" after decades of notes and hard decisions already made."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "This is NOT a crisis response team. The flood, the heatwave, the hurricane are not here yet. You are to make them less threatening, not start evacuating people right now."
msgstr "This is NOT a crisis response team. The flood, the heatwave, the hurricane are not here yet. You are to make them less threatening, not start evacuating people right now."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "The \"accessibility\" means three things: access of an average citizen to the infrastructure (a shelter maybe?), access of poorer / less fortunate residents to protenctions in their district, and of course access of the disabled citizens to things they need, as wheelchair-bound people will really struggle with knee-high floods."
msgstr "The \"accessibility\" means three things: access of an average citizen to the infrastructure (a shelter maybe?), access of poorer / less fortunate residents to protenctions in their district, and of course access of the disabled citizens to things they need, as wheelchair-bound people will really struggle with knee-high floods."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "Will this mean abandoning districts and forcible relocations, or worse, climate ghettos?"
msgstr "Will this mean abandoning districts and forcible relocations, or worse, climate ghettos?"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "Assuming the team has access to all the required data, scientists, meteorologists, city archives: how many different kinds of climate threats can they protect us from? What will help with heatwaves, what with floods, hurricanes?"
msgstr "Assuming the team has access to all the required data, scientists, meteorologists, city archives: how many different kinds of climate threats can they protect us from? What will help with heatwaves, what with floods, hurricanes?"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "What prices are considered too steep to pay? Are we going to surrender historical sites, places of remembrance? Are we okay with destroying a flood shaft and flooding a nature reserve to protect the population?"
msgstr "What prices are considered too steep to pay? Are we going to surrender historical sites, places of remembrance? Are we okay with destroying a flood shaft and flooding a nature reserve to protect the population?"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "How does the background of the team members play into that? Who already lives in a \"safe\", sutstainable tower, radiating pride and confidence, who clings to their family house in the suburbs, who cannot afford leaving a dangerous building which will not survive the next cataclysm?"
msgstr "How does the background of the team members play into that? Who already lives in a \"safe\", sutstainable tower, radiating pride and confidence, who clings to their family house in the suburbs, who cannot afford leaving a dangerous building which will not survive the next cataclysm?"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "What time-scale are we talking about? Are we okay with cheaper protections that will last a year, are we going for 5 years, a decade, or more?"
msgstr "What time-scale are we talking about? Are we okay with cheaper protections that will last a year, are we going for 5 years, a decade, or more?"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "How do we communicate it to the population, not to appear as despots choosing one group over another?"
msgstr "How do we communicate it to the population, not to appear as despots choosing one group over another?"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "What if we fail, what if we prepared for a flood and an unexpected heatwave rolls over, killing thousands? How do team members deal with guilt, do they accept the blame? Deny it?"
msgstr "What if we fail, what if we prepared for a flood and an unexpected heatwave rolls over, killing thousands? How do team members deal with guilt, do they accept the blame? Deny it?"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "A good book on the social infrastructure and the challenges of urban planning: https://www.goodreads.com/en/book/show/37707827 , with some tl;dr in https://99percentinvisible.org/episode/palaces-for-the-people/"
msgstr "A good book on the social infrastructure and the challenges of urban planning: https://www.goodreads.com/en/book/show/37707827 , with some tl;dr in https://99percentinvisible.org/episode/palaces-for-the-people/"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "https://reasonstobecheerful.world/waal-river-flooding-project/"
msgstr "https://reasonstobecheerful.world/waal-river-flooding-project/"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "https://www.preventionweb.net/news/germany-2021-floods-10-recommendations-resilience"
msgstr "https://www.preventionweb.net/news/germany-2021-floods-10-recommendations-resilience"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/features/2021-12-18/how-hamburg-learned-to-live-with-rising-water"
msgstr "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/features/2021-12-18/how-hamburg-learned-to-live-with-rising-water"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "https://www.archdaily.com/993434/can-architecture-and-urban-planning-fight-back-against-climate-change has some sources, but also a lot of \"fake\" solutions"
msgstr "https://www.archdaily.com/993434/can-architecture-and-urban-planning-fight-back-against-climate-change has some sources, but also a lot of \"fake\" solutions"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/seeds/the-refugee-camp/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Refugee Camp"
msgstr "Il Campo Profughi"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-refugee-camp/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> There is a full-fledged town built from a refugee camp which was set up there two decades ago. The inhabitants speak their own creole, a mix of more than five languages, and have very shaky relationships with their neighboring communities or states, each of which considers it a lawless territory and might be plotting to take over.\n"
msgstr "> Un campo profughi istituito una ventina d’anni fa diventa un villaggio vero e proprio. I suoi abitanti parlano un dialetto nato da cinque o più lingue e hanno relazioni instabili con le comunità e gli stati limitrofi, ciascuno dei quali considera il villaggio una zona fuori da ogni giurisdizione e mira ad acquisirne il controllo.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-refugee-camp/index.en.md
msgid "[Solarpunk Prompts Podcast Episode](https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-refugee-camp)"
msgstr "[Episodio Solarpunk Prompts Podcast](https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-refugee-camp)"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-refugee-camp/index.en.md
msgid "[Transcript](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-Refugee-Camp)"
msgstr "[Trascrizione (ENG)](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-Refugee-Camp)"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Reservists"
msgstr "I Riservisti"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> As a disaster strikes, completely overwhelming several communities, a group of friends is called back into service as first responders. Each of their lives took a different path since the Service, but as they scramble to remember their training - as flood control, epidemic trackers, trauma psychologists or radio technicians - they feel like one unit again. Meeting new kids, straight from the mandatory training everyone goes through - will they become their mentors, or struggle opening up to greenhorns?\n"
msgstr "> Quando un disastro colpisce, soverchiando varie comunità, un gruppo di amici viene convocato a prestare servizio come primo soccorso. Ciascuna delle loro vite ha preso una direzione diversa dopo il Servizio, ma mentre cercano di ricordare la propria formazione (come arginare un'alluvione, tracciare un'epidemia, affrontare i traumi dei sopravvissuti e operare strumenti radio) riscoprono come fare gruppo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "There is A LOT of baggage coming with the idea of a military service, the indocrination of the military, nationalism, destroying the individualism, discriminating against queer people, hiding sexual abuse etc. Let's acknowledge that and instead of \"re-forging existing militaries\" (as is episode #11) let's focus on something else: life after service."
msgstr "There is A LOT of baggage coming with the idea of a military service, the indocrination of the military, nationalism, destroying the individualism, discriminating against queer people, hiding sexual abuse etc. Let's acknowledge that and instead of \"re-forging existing militaries\" (as is episode #11) let's focus on something else: life after service."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "Let's imagine that after finishing high school, but before going to the University, every person in our society goes through 2 years of training and climate service. It doesn't matter what gender they are, or if they are disabled: they get assigned to a specialization and they learn how to help their community and society in some way. They can be first responders, they can be electricians, logisticians, kindergardeners, forest rangers, flood experts od epidemic effort coordinators. They are not professionals - of course, they can align their careers along their training - but they are the \"service members\"."
msgstr "Let's imagine that after finishing high school, but before going to the University, every person in our society goes through 2 years of training and climate service. It doesn't matter what gender they are, or if they are disabled: they get assigned to a specialization and they learn how to help their community and society in some way. They can be first responders, they can be electricians, logisticians, kindergardeners, forest rangers, flood experts od epidemic effort coordinators. They are not professionals - of course, they can align their careers along their training - but they are the \"service members\"."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "This gives people their first skillset, but at the same time assures that everyone in a given region can help in case of a catastrophe. In case of a given kind of help needed, people with the right expertise are called for, no matter where in life are they now - whether hairdressers, engineers or politicians."
msgstr "This gives people their first skillset, but at the same time assures that everyone in a given region can help in case of a catastrophe. In case of a given kind of help needed, people with the right expertise are called for, no matter where in life are they now - whether hairdressers, engineers or politicians."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "They were equal once, within their \"unit\", and they will be equal once more, standing at the flood embankments."
msgstr "They were equal once, within their \"unit\", and they will be equal once more, standing at the flood embankments."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "What's important, this prompt is not set DURING their initial training and service (as per #11), but years after, when people are mobilized again."
msgstr "What's important, this prompt is not set DURING their initial training and service (as per #11), but years after, when people are mobilized again."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "This gives us A LOT in terms of worldbuilding:"
msgstr "This gives us A LOT in terms of worldbuilding:"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "Everyone has been through a similar experience. This gives them a friend-group for life, some more empathy for people from vastly different paths of life, but can also result in some tribalism."
msgstr "Everyone has been through a similar experience. This gives them a friend-group for life, some more empathy for people from vastly different paths of life, but can also result in some tribalism."

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "Are there sports teams or political factions based on the \"service groups\"? The Firemen versus The Radio Guys?"
msgstr "Are there sports teams or political factions based on the \"service groups\"? The Firemen versus The Radio Guys?"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "Instead of being indoctrinated into patriotism and nationalism, our service members share a bond of saving lives and helping others in their own way. They might bring a lot of different and conflicting ideologies to the table, but this is something that connects them all."
msgstr "Instead of being indoctrinated into patriotism and nationalism, our service members share a bond of saving lives and helping others in their own way. They might bring a lot of different and conflicting ideologies to the table, but this is something that connects them all."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "As with current military reservists, people will be called for trainings once every year, or several years. If they weren't a group of friends and a small community then, they probably will be."
msgstr "As with current military reservists, people will be called for trainings once every year, or several years. If they weren't a group of friends and a small community then, they probably will be."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "What in case of a drama? If Casey told Tom she really hates them, can they work well together under a lot of pressure, during a cataclysm? There must be some procedures in place for that!"
msgstr "What in case of a drama? If Casey told Tom she really hates them, can they work well together under a lot of pressure, during a cataclysm? There must be some procedures in place for that!"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "Will they naturally navigate to live close together, potentially making the whole social structure more fragile? The service members are supposed to be spread more-or-less uniformly in each region!"
msgstr "Will they naturally navigate to live close together, potentially making the whole social structure more fragile? The service members are supposed to be spread more-or-less uniformly in each region!"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "In our Solarpunk world we want to imagine full transparency, so no \"buying easier spots\" in a team. Everyone gets a specialization along their skills and limitations and everyone is equal."
msgstr "In our Solarpunk world we want to imagine full transparency, so no \"buying easier spots\" in a team. Everyone gets a specialization along their skills and limitations and everyone is equal."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "How does a mobilization look like? What if someone is sick, pregnant, or cannot leave their position - for example at the power plant?"
msgstr "How does a mobilization look like? What if someone is sick, pregnant, or cannot leave their position - for example at the power plant?"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "From a very human side: how does mobilization look like? Is it a thrill, \"me and my friends are going to save some asses?\""
msgstr "From a very human side: how does mobilization look like? Is it a thrill, \"me and my friends are going to save some asses?\""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "While there might be a lot to explain in this prompt, I think the story itself would be really fun and enjoyable both to write and read. The action, the dramatism is right there, and it's full of potential \"flashbacks\" to regular lives in a Solarpunk world."
msgstr "While there might be a lot to explain in this prompt, I think the story itself would be really fun and enjoyable both to write and read. The action, the dramatism is right there, and it's full of potential \"flashbacks\" to regular lives in a Solarpunk world."

#. type: Title ###
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Service Members vs Volunteers"
msgstr "Service Members vs Volunteers"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "The focus on this prompt can go both ways and I think both are equally interesting. The first is the mandated Service that a lot of people might not like, as it's \"too authoritarian\", while the latter is just Volunteering, which assumes that people got the necessary training on their own (like https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Icelandic_Association_for_Search_and_Rescue or Volunteer Firefighters)."
msgstr "The focus on this prompt can go both ways and I think both are equally interesting. The first is the mandated Service that a lot of people might not like, as it's \"too authoritarian\", while the latter is just Volunteering, which assumes that people got the necessary training on their own (like https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Icelandic_Association_for_Search_and_Rescue or Volunteer Firefighters)."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "The very heart of the prompt is people who are leading normal lives until they are called for help - and their social dynamics, since it's what creates the story. Emphasizing how volunteering works right now could help the listeners imagine that, but I also think that imagining a huge cultural shift where everybody shares this experience is important."
msgstr "The very heart of the prompt is people who are leading normal lives until they are called for help - and their social dynamics, since it's what creates the story. Emphasizing how volunteering works right now could help the listeners imagine that, but I also think that imagining a huge cultural shift where everybody shares this experience is important."

#. type: Title ###
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generational Shift"
msgstr "Generational Shift"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "An interesting aspect of the story would be the first year / generation of the Reservists and how alien, oppressive the program might feel - set against the culture 20+ years later, where it's normalized, and everyone shares the duty / responsibility of the Service."
msgstr "An interesting aspect of the story would be the first year / generation of the Reservists and how alien, oppressive the program might feel - set against the culture 20+ years later, where it's normalized, and everyone shares the duty / responsibility of the Service."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/seeds/the-ship/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Ship"
msgstr "La Nave"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-ship/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> There is a modern cargo ship made with sails and solar panels, trying to replace the oil guzzlers of old and connect the world again. It is crewed by sailors old and young, engineers maintaining some experimental solutions, and some communities trying to travel in old container-houses. They have a lot on their plate.\n"
msgstr "> Una nave mercantile con vele e pannelli solari cerca di sostituire i titani del mare e connettere nuovamente il mondo. L’equipaggio, composto da marinai di ogni età e ingegneri che sperimentano nuove soluzioni, incontra rifugiati che cercano di viaggiare in case-container.\n"

